``` =====================================================================
    LDAP failures on domain controllers
    Finds: bind/connection errors, rejected or insecure binds, channel
    binding failures, and LDAPS TLS handshake failures.

    PREREQUISITES
    1. LDAP diagnostic logging on every DC. Without it, 1216/2889/3039
       never fire and you only get daily summaries with no client IPs.
         HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NTDS\Diagnostics
         16 LDAP Interface Events = 2 (DWORD)
    2. Directory Service log forwarded from the DCs (UF inputs.conf):
         [WinEventLog://Directory Service]
         disabled = 0
    3. Classic WinEventLog rendering (Message field). With XmlWinEventLog,
       these NTDS events store their data in unnamed Data elements, so the
       rex extractions below need rewriting.

    EVENT REFERENCE
    1216         LDAP connection closed on error (per client, IP + error)
    2887         Daily count of unsigned or cleartext binds
    2888         Daily count of binds rejected because signing is required
    2889         Per-client unsigned SASL bind (type 0) or cleartext
                 simple bind (type 1)
    3039         Per-client channel binding token failure (LDAPS)
    3040, 3041   Daily channel binding summaries
    36874, 36887, 36888
                 Schannel TLS handshake failures. No client IP is logged,
                 so correlate by time with 1216 or firewall logs.
    The summary events fire once per DC per day. Per-client detail comes
    from 1216, 2889 and 3039.

    COMMON 1216 ERROR VALUES
    8009030C     Logon failure (bad credentials)
    80090346     Bad channel bindings (appears once CBT enforcement is on)
    ===================================================================== ```

index=wineventlog

``` SCOPE: keep exactly one of Option A or Option B active.

    Option A (active): every DC whose host value contains the domain or
    naming pattern. The tstats subsearch returns only hosts that send
    Directory Service logs, which means real DCs, so Schannel noise from
    member servers stays out. Change contoso here to target another domain. ```
[| tstats count where index=wineventlog source="WinEventLog:Directory Service" host="*contoso*" by host | fields host]

``` Option B: explicit list of DCs. Wildcards work, e.g. contosodc*.
    To use it, comment out Option A and remove the backticks below. ```
```host IN (dc01, dc02, dc03)```

``` Events of interest. The Directory Service log only exists on DCs.
    Schannel events are in the System log on every server, which is why
    the scope above limits results to DCs. ```
((source="WinEventLog:Directory Service" EventCode IN (1216,2887,2888,2889,3039,3040,3041))
 OR (source="WinEventLog:System" SourceName="Schannel" EventCode IN (36874,36887,36888)))

``` Option C: use when host values are short names without the domain in
    them. Comment out Option A, then remove the backticks on the next line.
    This is slower, and member-server Schannel events get through unless
    you also use Option B. ```
```| search ComputerName="*.contoso.*"```

``` Extract client details from the event message. ```
| rex field=Message "Client IP(?: address)?:\s+(?<client_ip>\d{1,3}(?:\.\d{1,3}){3})"
| rex field=Message "authenticate as:\s+(?<identity>\S+)"
| rex field=Message "Binding Type:\s+(?<bind_type>\d)"
| rex field=Message "Error value:\s+(?<ldap_error>[^\r\n]+)"

``` Give each event a readable failure type. ```
| eval failure=case(
    EventCode=1216, "Bind/connection failed",
    EventCode=2888, "Rejected insecure binds (summary)",
    EventCode=2889 AND bind_type=0, "Unsigned SASL bind",
    EventCode=2889 AND bind_type=1, "Cleartext simple bind",
    EventCode=3039, "Channel binding failure",
    in(EventCode,"2887","3040","3041"), "Insecure bind summary",
    SourceName="Schannel", "LDAPS TLS handshake failure")

``` stats drops rows with a null by-field. Without fillnull, the summary
    and Schannel events (no IP or identity) would disappear. ```
| fillnull value="-" client_ip identity ldap_error

| stats count min(_time) as first_seen max(_time) as last_seen
        values(host) as dcs by failure client_ip identity ldap_error
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - count
